New features:
- Implemented voice chat
- Implemented support for TLS-encrypted servers in FeralTweaks
- Added four unused emotes (/yes, /no, /eat, /scared) that were left over from the original game but were never unused (NOTE THAT WE CANNOT FIX BROKEN EMOTES, THESE FOUR ARENT SUPPORTED BY ALL AVATARS)
- Implemented tags: kind of like permission groups, can be used for name prefixes, name colors and module use
- Implemented save prefixes: player save settings can now specify prefixes to use in display names
- Implemented prefix hiding: players can choose to hide their prefixes via commands
- Implemented chat proxying (use >help for a list of commands ingame related to this feature)
- Implemented the Edge text filter, this replaces the old EmuFeral text filter, this new filter is vastly superior to the older version
- Implemented Private Instances! You can find the feature in the Discord bot and in ingame chat commands!
- Implemented like rewards for twiggle builders
- Implemented MMO rooms

New commands:
- Implemented a general 'shutdownserver' command that doesnt trigger a update call (still says its updating on the client unless its FeralTweaks, this is a client limitation)
- Implemented renaming of GCs via the gcrename (gcr) command
- Implemented gclistmembers (gclm) command
- Implemented coordsof, a moderator command to show a player's coordinates
- Implemented tp, a moderator command to teleport to players or coordinates
- Implemented tpall, a moderator command to teleport every player in a room to a player or coordinates
- Implemented tpserverto, a moderator command that practically yanks everyone in the entire game to a specific player
- Implemented tptosanctuary, a moderator command to teleport to sanctuaries
- Implemented gatherallplayers and endgathering, these are moderator commands to temporarily disengage the room instancing system and teleport everyone into the same room
- Implemented a dice roll command (>roll) for roleplay purposes
- Implemented a player count command (>listplayers) for regular players that shows how many are ingame

New quests:
- Ultimate Refreshment

New functionality:
- Implemented the ability to create new Decree Board entries
- Implemented a quest plugin system, this allows for creation of quest server logic
- Added event: InteractionWorldSetupEvent: called when the world's interactable objects are being gathered, use this to register custom objects to a level
- Added event: InteractionStateChangeEvent: called when the state of any interactable object changes
- Added event: QuestStartEvent: called when a player starts a quest
- Added event: QuestCompleteEvent: called when a player completes a quest
- Added event: QuestTaskCompletedEvent: called when a player completes quest tasks
- Added event: QuestObjectiveCompletedEvent: called when a player completes quest objectives
- Backported the Edge/Nexus EventBus to improve module API
- Backported the Edge module system to improve module loading

QoL Changes:
- Added an unread counter in world chat for when in GCs or DMs
- Made it that PM message notifications arent processed as unreads by the notification system
- Made it that gameplay item reward notifications arent processed as unreads by the notification system [ TO FIX, BUGGY ATM ]
- Made it that gameplay notifications such as quests arent processed as unreads by the notification system
- Fixed unread counter not showing correct amount of unread messages
- Implemented chat formatting (minimal markdown-like syntax)
- Made it so that chat scrolls down even if in other channels
- Improved chat bubbles by making them semi-scroll instead of replacing the full text when it has too many messages
- Made some improvements to gliding logic and added flapping! (press F to flap while gliding)
- Made it that the teleport-in/teleport-out animations are played on login/logout for other players
- Made it so that you can have multiple clothing items of the same category (PC ONLY)
- Increased decal resolution to 2048 for high, 1024 for mid and left low on 512
- Added a lot more eye and pupil types, all NPC eye and pupil types are available for avatars now too
- Added 'no eye' eye type for all avatars
- Added a 'typing' status in chat
- Reimplemented avatar blinking [ BUG: CAN RANDOMLY FAIL ]

Fixes in the server:
- Fixed online player counter on the API website
- Fixed display name sync for when permissions are updated
- Improved synchronization practices for thread-unsafe operations, this increases performance and lessens load impact
- Improved packet reading logic, enhancing server performance
- Fixed server error loop when players change while retrieving the player list
- Fixed duplicate lockpick consumption when hitting the lock rings
- Fixed date/time formatting issues that were causing time desyncs
- Improved chat performance by overhaulling sendmessage handling, the room system and general networking logic
- Properly implemented trade chat, its no longer a DM channel but a transient channel thats closed when trade ends
- Fixed sync resetting the last action to default when its not a action type packet
- Fixed the moderation log not showing the chat message when autofilter mutes players
- Fixed find player crashing the game when the target player has not used the social services before
- Fixed player actions (sitting etc) not correctly syncing when using the editor
- Fixed player sync causing action resets for other players when the sync packet in question isnt a action/emote packet
- Fixed player card, display names and experience server calls randomly failing
- Fixed players not receiving status updates about friends that are coming online
- Fixed quest item randomization breaking down causing eg. feed the tree to bug out
- Fixed harvest trackers progressing the quest while its not started
- Fixed issues with the block system in chat
- Fixed initial sync coordinates being off
- Fixed GCs showing as 'offline' in chat
- Fixed the avatar look save bug and implemented a failsafe to correct broken look selection
- Fixed broken loot spawning
- Fixed pardon moderation event not being dispatched

Fixes in the client:
- Fixed chat randomly failing to connect at world join [WIP, only need new protocol]
- Fixed chart patches not being picked up by all of the game
- Fixed chart patches not being correctly parsed, fixed new chart definitions not working
- Fixed autologin errors preventing further regular logins
- POTENTIALLY fixed the infamous 10-XXX (critical error updating feral) bug (unable to reproduce, theoretical remedy in place, may be resolved but unable to trigger it) -- NOT FIXED ENTIRELY (NOTE TO SELF)
- Fixed login loading screen transition randomly failing to fade in
- Fixed chat stripping <> while noparse takes care of that
- Fixed creation of assets not functioning correctly
- Fixed group chats not being resized properly
- Fixed the favorite 'Player has joined you' spam bug

Visual fixes in the client:
- Fixed off-centered dragon spark, its now correctly centered
- Fixed the emote wheel not showing all of the primary emotes (note that the new four emotes are only usable via slash commands) [ TO FIX: INITIAL RENDERING STILL OFF ]
- Fixed the floating rocks animations not working during events
- Fixed NPC head rotation not functioning [ TO FIX: FINICKY AF ]

New client content/functionality:
- Dragons and Shinigami can now 'glide' without wings
- Added a 'no legs' body mod for dragons

Other changes:
- Made it that the Centuria APIs arent blocked by CORS
- DMs/GCs now allow infinite chat history, instead, the server checks daily if a private chat is inactive for 2 months, if so, it deletes it
- Refactored server resources, they are now properly structured
- Added a 'reason' argument to the updateshutdown command
- Added a 'reason' argument to the startmaintenance command
- Made it that Phoenixes can now have 'no wings' in experience mode
- Increased general scaling options to allow larger and smaller sizes
- Increased jump force (a fourth of extra force)
- Made it that the server will always load save settings from the save manager if the active save is present in the configuration unless overridden

Changes to loot and resources:
- Increased skyjelly drop rate
- Increased pyrite cicada drop rate


HEADS-UP!
Centuria/EmuFeral now has a room management system! This means you will not always be in the same room as other players!
Use the social system to get to other players if you arent in the same room as them. The server prioritizes rooms with followed players over other rooms unless they are 'full',
but you can always teleport to your friends.


